Why Is Demand Increasing
Renewable Integration: CCGT plants provide flexible and dispatchable electricity that can complement intermittent solar and wind generation.
High Efficiency: Modern combined-cycle systems can achieve efficiency levels above 60%, improving fuel economics and reducing emissions per unit of electricity.
Grid Modernization: Replacement of aging thermal assets and growing electricity demand are encouraging investment in efficient gas-fired generation.

Industry Watch: Hydrogen-Ready Turbines Support the Energy Transition
CCGT technology is increasingly being developed around fuel flexibility, higher efficiency, digital monitoring, and hydrogen compatibility. Manufacturers are investing in advanced turbine designs and service solutions that allow power producers to improve performance today while preparing assets for lower-carbon fuels.

